1.3.3-snapshot
  An offline cull crash fix, respawn counters repaired to the live count, attachment caps
    Smart Sanitizer now repairs a corrupted respawn counter to the number of squads alive, which ends the runaway respawn at that smart terrain on the next pass.
    Inventory Guard gives loose attachments a separate cap and keeps the one that fits a stalker's gun, and a rare offline cull crash is gone.

  Offline Guard
    - Fixed a rare crash when X-Ray gave a wiped squad's id to another object while a cull pass was still running.

  Smart Sanitizer
    - Changed the repair of a corrupted respawn counter from 0 to the smart terrain's real count of live squads.
      A reset to 0 let the surviving squads drive the counter negative again on their next death, and the smart kept spawning squads without limit every few minutes.
      The repair ends that runaway on the next pass. Squads already spawned stay, and the population guards cull them over time.

  Inventory Guard
    - Fixed a scope or silencer you handed to a stalker vanishing when he carried a spare gun. Attachments counted against the spare weapon cap, and now have a separate cap of 2.
    - Changed the cull to keep the scope or silencer that fits a stalker's pistol or rifle, apart from his 2 spares.

  Update check
    - Added an update check. On the first save load of each launch the mod asks GitHub for its latest release, during the loading screen.
      A newer version shows at the foot of the MCM page, and in a PDA message once a day. It needs xlibs 1.10.1.
    - Added Check for update to the Development page, which runs the same check right away.

1.3.2
  Scripted and quest-target protection, a higher online limit, kept gear, lighter trims
    Online Guard protects squads another script steers and the target of your current quest, and the default online limit rises from 80 to 120 NPCs.
    Inventory Guard keeps binoculars, night vision and armour plates, no longer touches traders, and trims a heavy hoarder in a single walk.
    Other things you will notice. A hoarder clears over the next cycles, the platform line prints to the engine log, and the mod needs xlibs 1.9.0.

  Online Guard
    - Added Protect scripted NPCs, on by default. A squad another script steers, such as an outpost service at his post, a chase target or a mod-spawned guard, is no longer culled by either guard.
      An outpost trader survives population pressure. Turn it off for the hardest culling, which then removes script-managed squads too.
    - Fixed the guards culling an active quest target, which failed the quest as soon as the cleanup ran.
      The NPC, mutant or squad marked on your map for the current objective is now protected, beside the task-giver and bounty or hostage protection.
    - Changed the default online population limit from 80 to 120 NPCs. Custom settings stay as they are.

  Inventory Guard
    - Fixed the trim taking gear an NPC should keep. Binoculars counted as a weapon and night vision as a device, and armour plates fell outside every kept category. Each now keeps one.
    - Improved inventory trim performance. The trim walks an inventory once instead of twice, with a cap on the items it reads.
    - Removed the trader stock purge. The trade flow bounds trader, mechanic, medic and barman stock, and the guard no longer scans a trader at all.
    - Fixed a heavy hoarder clearing only part of his surplus, then waiting a full cooldown. He now rescans each cycle until clean.

  General
    - Added the platform status line to the engine log at startup.
    - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.9.0.

1.3.1
  Inventory Guard, the trader stock purge, a separate sanitizer toggle
    Inventory Guard is a new tab. It bounds what NPCs hoard so anti-loot addons are no longer needed, moved from AlifeBalance with the same behavior.
    The trader stock purge releases worn-out stock from traders, and Smart Sanitizer runs on a separate toggle, apart from the Online Guard.

  Offline Guard
    - Fixed the guard re-processing a crowded region it could not thin any further, which ran background work each pass with nothing to remove.

  Smart Sanitizer
    - Changed the sanitizer to run on a separate setting. Save-crash protection stays on when the Online Guard is off.

  Inventory Guard
    - Added Inventory Guard, moved from AlifeBalance, where it was Inventory Balance, with the same behavior.
      A scanner walks online stalkers one per frame, releases the surplus above each category's limit, and rescans each NPC at most twice per game day.
      Companions, story characters and named NPCs are never touched, and service NPCs matched by role skip the trim, runtime-spawned ones included.
      The limits live in ag_inventory_policy.ltx, overridable through DLTX, which replaces ab_inventory_policy.ltx.
    - Added the trader stock purge. Weapons, outfits and helmets below a condition threshold leave the stock of traders, mechanics, medics and barmen.
      A long selling session no longer piles junk stock toward the engine's object cap. Equipped gear, quest items, consumables, ammo and money stay.

  General
    - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.8.3.

1.3.0
  Offline Guard, companions always protected, platform status, Russian strings
    Offline Guard is a new tab that caps A-Life density on the other maps. A crowded hub no longer floods the online count when you arrive.
    Companions are always protected from culling, online and offline, and the MCM footer shows a live xlibs and exe compatibility status.

  Online Guard
    - Changed companions to stay protected from culling whatever the task toggle says.

  Offline Guard
    - Added Offline Guard. A light scan checks offline squads by position and thins any region over its trigger to its target.
      Named NPCs, commanders and protected squads are never removed, and every squad keeps its commander.

  General
    - Added the platform status line to the MCM, with a live xlibs and exe compatibility result.
    - Fixed an outdated xlibs raising an error at load. The dependency check now shows the update-xlibs message.
    - Added Russian strings for the Offline Guard tab, the cleanup tips and the MCM reset confirmation.
    - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.8.2.

1.2.7
  AOEngine support, the modded exes check, fewer engine warnings
    AOEngine is supported, and the load check now stops the game with a message when it finds neither demonized 20250908 or newer nor AOEngine.
    A creature despawning during a cleanup no longer floods the log with warnings, and the MCM reset button sits at the bottom of Development.

  Online Guard
    - Fixed a burst of "trying to use a destroyed object" warnings when a creature despawned during a cleanup cycle.

  Development
    - Changed the Reset button to sit at the bottom of the Development tab.

  General
    - Added AOEngine support and the modded exes check.
    - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.7.7.

1.2.6
  A fix for the MCM reset crash
    Reset to defaults no longer crashes on some exes, and a warning above the button asks you to save or discard pending changes first.

  Development
    - Fixed Reset to defaults crashing on some exes.
    - Added a warning above the reset button to save or discard pending MCM changes first.

1.2.5
  Task-giver protection, the MCM tab split, the reset button and the cleanup sound
    Task givers are no longer culled, and PDA Taskboard tasks no longer fail when a cleanup runs. The MCM splits into Online Guard, Smart Sanitizer and Development.
    Cleanup messages read as the Zone itself, with a sound cue. The manual buttons are gone, because the cycles run by themselves.

  Online Guard
    - Fixed cleanup releasing task givers, which failed PDA Taskboard tasks. Taskboard squad members and lone task givers are both protected.
    - Fixed crashes around stale squad references and recycled server ids during a release.
    - Changed the PDA cleanup messages to 3 lines in the voice of the Zone.
    - Added Notification sound, a short ambient cue when cleanup fires.
    - Removed the Show status, Delete common, Delete all squads and Force cleanup buttons. The cycles run by themselves.

  Smart Sanitizer
    - Changed the sanitizer settings into a separate tab.
    - Removed the Sanitize now button. The periodic pass handles it.

  Development
    - Added Reset to defaults, which restores every setting in one click.

  General
    - Changed the MCM tabs to Online Guard, Smart Sanitizer and Development. Old settings no longer apply.
    - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.7.1.

1.2.0
  Smart Sanitizer, against save crashes and endless respawns
    Corrupted respawn counters on smart terrains get repaired by Smart Sanitizer. They cause save crashes and endless spawn loops, usually after a spawner or despawner mod.

  Development
    - Added Smart Sanitizer. It clamps negative or non-numeric respawn counters, once on load and periodically during play.
      A negative counter crashed the game on save, and made its smart terrain spawn squads without end.
      The load pass runs before the respawn loop reads the counters restored from the save.
    - Added the Smart Sanitizer toggle, its interval slider and a sanitize button, with English and Russian strings.

  General
    - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.4.0.

1.1.1
  Vanilla exe support
    The population scan no longer needs the demonized exes. AlifeGuard runs on vanilla Anomaly 1.5.3, demonized, demonized MT and AOEngine.

  General
    - Fixed the population scan crashing without the demonized exes. It now walks online objects through xlibs.
    - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.3.0.

1.1.0
  Squad-aware culling, fair removals across factions, and a hysteresis buffer
    The guard now thins squads member by member, commanders last, and spreads removals evenly across factions and mutant types.
    A buffer between the trigger and the target stops it from culling again at once, and every protection works at squad level.
    Other things you will notice. Scripted squads go last, companion squads are protected, and the MCM gains a Development tab.

  General
    - Changed culling to work on squads. Members go first and commanders last, and a squad survives a cleanup.
    - Added round-robin removal across factions and mutant types. No single faction loses everything first.
    - Added 4 priority tiers, from unscripted members to scripted commanders. Squads that AlifePlus, Warfare or Guards Spawner steer go last.
    - Added the hysteresis buffer, a gap between the trigger and the cull target.
    - Changed protection to work on the whole squad: story, trader, task giver, companion, and bounty or hostage.
    - Added protection for companion squads, where only individual companions were protected before.
    - Fixed named NPCs who are not their squad's commander being culled.
    - Added toggles for squad culling and round-robin fairness, and a buffer slider.
    - Improved performance. Squad-level checks replace the per-NPC scans.
    - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.7.

  Development
    - Added the Development tab, with the diagnostics, the population reset and a log level list in place of the debug toggle.

1.0.10
  The xlibs 1.2.5 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.2.5, and the load check accepts any newer compatible version.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.5.

1.0.9
  Frame-spread cleanup, a higher default limit, and task target protection
    The cleanup now releases one NPC per frame, and assault, bounty, hostage and delivery squads are never culled.
    Other things you will notice. The default limit rises from 70 to 80, the MCM shows a banner, and the Russian MCM reads correctly again.

  - Changed entity removal to spread across frames, one per frame, with no stutter.
  - Added protection for task target squads. Assault, bounty, hostage and delivery squads are never released.
  - Fixed Delete common squads removing bounty and hostage quest targets.
  - Fixed a crash in the squad release on stale ids after a repopulate.
  - Changed the default online limit from 70 to 80.
  - Added the MCM banner, and the mod and xlibs versions to the log at startup.
  - Fixed the Russian MCM text, which showed broken characters.
  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.4.

1.0.8
  The xlibs 1.2.3 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.2.3, and the load check accepts any newer compatible version.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.3.

1.0.7
  The xlibs 1.2.1 requirement
    This release runs on xlibs 1.2.1, and the load check asks for that exact version.

  - Changed the xlibs requirement to 1.2.1.

1.0.6
  A higher default limit, faster settings reads, and the MCM reset button
    The default online limit rises from 40 to 70, and the MCM reset button restores every setting.

  - Changed the default online limit from 40 to 70.
  - Improved settings performance.
  - Added support for the MCM reset button, and cleaned up the MCM labels.

1.0.5
  An exact xlibs version check
    The load check now matches the xlibs version exactly, where it used to compare the version as text.

  - Fixed the xlibs check comparing versions as text. It now asks for the exact version.

1.0.4
  The task-giver protection fix
    Task givers from the A-Life simulation are protected again, and the debug log names every protection decision.

  - Fixed task givers from the A-Life simulation going unprotected. The task giver id belongs to the squad, not the NPC.
  - Added debug traces for every protection decision and every released section.

1.0.3
  The xlibs check and the Russian translation
    From this release the mod checks the xlibs version at load, and the MCM reads in Russian.

  - Added the xlibs check at load, with a message when xlibs is missing or outdated.
  - Added the Russian translation.

1.0.2
  Bounty and hostage protection
    Bounty and hostage task targets are no longer released.

  - Fixed bounty and hostage task targets being released.

1.0.1
  A fix for console log spam
    The guard no longer floods the console while it walks and releases entities.

  - Fixed log spam from alive() and release calls on objects that are not creatures.
  - Fixed a missing default for the check interval.

1.0.0
  An online entity limiter
    The first release keeps the number of online NPCs under a limit by releasing the farthest ones back to offline simulation.

  - Added the online guard, which removes NPCs by distance once the online count passes the limit.
  - Added protection for traders, companions, story characters and task NPCs.
  - Added MCM buttons for status, cleanup, delete common squads and delete all squads.
  - Added PDA notifications for each cleanup, and debug logging.
